  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was affected by pre-Columbus Day booking patterns, but the underlying story is mixed and deserves attention.\n\nPort Washington is the concern. Yesterday's 47% revenue drop reflects a real capacity miss\u2014only 2 groomers with zero bather support, producing $512/groomer against a $460 trailing baseline. The damage cascaded: core grooms down 54%, add-ons down 55% despite flat attach rate, and retail down 24%. Week-to-date appointments are down 21%. However, MTD sits flat versus last September after DOW adjustment (+6% appointments offsetting a 4.5% revenue shortfall), so the month isn't lost. The risk: if tomorrow's single-groomer schedule repeats, the trend inverts fast.\n\nHicksville is running well. MTD revenue is up 26% and DOW-adjusted actual outperformed expectation by 1.6%. Yesterday's add-on collapse (33% attach vs 54% baseline) is a red flag for upsell discipline, but appointments are up 9% week-to-date and $/groomer-day ($446) remains above prior-month baseline. Glen Cove's opening week shows promise\u2014$452/groomer well above its 30-day baseline of $274\u2014though the sample is tiny.\n\nYou should be proud of year-to-date performance: up 38% revenue and 37% appointments across the core two locations. The pattern worth naming: both Port Washington and Hicksville are suffering bather hour gaps (Port at zero vs 5.8-day average; Hicksville chronically at zero). This is suppressing throughput and retail. Tomorrow's schedule\u20145 groomers at Port Washington with 15 bather hours, 1 groomer at Hicksville with zero bathers\u2014needs to hold. Next seven days: 57 groomer-days across all locations with only 83 bather hours total.\n\n**Today Port Washington has 1 groomer and 15.0 bather hours; tomorrow 5 groomers with 15.0 bather hours; next 7 days 57 groomer-days (Port 35, Hicksville 22, Glen Cove 0) with 83 bather hours total.**"
